# Pre-deploy audit

Critical repairs from the live/dev comparison, code review and local production-build checks. All 93 pages pass structural, link and image comparisons; these functional issues survive those checks. Form tests were intercepted; no real submissions or payments were sent.

- [ ] **Bind the actual booking payload on every tour.** All 29 pages retain the sample's hidden tour name, `RINGS-EN` code, $425/$213 prices and `can-pay-online=true`. For example, Waitomo & Hobbiton should submit `WHOB-EN` and $525/$263. This misidentifies enquiries and can send tours into the wrong payment flow. Repair `web/src/lib/templates/tour.ts`, including hidden inputs and the online-payment flag.

- [ ] **Restore date selection for tours without a calendar.** `window.Tour` still identifies every page as Hobbiton with a TourAid code. The engine therefore locks the required date field even on the 13 tours with no calendar, preventing normal booking/enquiry submission. Bind the script data per tour; verify `/tour/puhoi-river-kayaking` permits manual date selection.

- [ ] **Replace Webflow processing for agent registration.** `/agents` has no external form action and still submits to `webflow.com/api/v1/form/...`. Webflow does not process forms on externally hosted exports. Connect a supported backend and verify delivery before cut-over. Source: `web/src/html/main.agents.html`; [Webflow documentation](https://help.webflow.com/hc/en-us/articles/33961341546899-Collect-form-submissions-on-exported-sites).

- [ ] **Restore the contact-form handler dependencies.** `/engine/webflow-form.js` imports `/modules/webflow-form.js` and `/modules/webflow-form-ipinfo.js`; both return 404 in dev and the production build. The Basin handler never initializes: an intercepted submission navigated away to Basin instead of following the configured `/thanks` flow. Bundle the dependencies and verify success, failure and redirect handling.

- [ ] **Move raw card entry on `/booking` to hosted checkout.** The inherited form collects the full card number and expiry in ordinary inputs and posts them to `navi.co.nz/tours/bookEnglishTours.php`, while third-party analytics/chat scripts run on the same page. Replace these fields with the hosted Windcave/PayPal payment flow so card details are entered at the payment provider.
